# Smoke tests

Project health checks via **`uv run tests smoke`** (catalpa-workspace-tooling v0.8.1+; `*.dev.localhost` healthcheck fix in v0.8.3+). [docs/SMOKE_TESTS.md](https://github.com/catalpainternational/catalpa-workspace-tooling/blob/main/docs/SMOKE_TESTS.md) in catalpa-workspace-tooling.

## When to suggest smoke

- User bumped **catalpa-workspace-tooling** or asks to validate a stack after changes
- User mentions smoke tests, PWA load check, or post-merge validation on **local dev**

## Setup (Django compose consumers)

1. **`[dependency-groups].smoke`** in consumer repo root `pyproject.toml` — not in shared vendor/submodule `pyproject.toml` if that would force unrelated lock churn
2. Tests live in **`{paths.frontend}/smoke/`** (from `tooling.yaml`)
3. One-time: `uv run playwright install chromium`

## Safe local run

```bash
uv run dk dev up -d          # if stack not running
uv run tests smoke --no-up    # skip compose up when stack is already up
```

Use **`--check-only`** for migration preflight without applying. Use **`--fresh-db`** for empty-DB migrate on an ephemeral database (local only).

## Do not

- Add `pytest` / `pytest-playwright` to shared submodule `pyproject.toml` when deps belong in the consumer repo only
- Run **`uv run tests smoke`** against **staging/prod** without explicit user confirmation (same bar as remote `dk`; see `remote-environments.mdc`)
- Decrypt or print deploy secrets to debug smoke failures

